<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:45:27Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a4eb609db7a52fb8d1cb9333b3dc6b71203805198f33ae17ca685cb4f7d56bf1</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Deutsche Bank under fire after internal documents made public</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfd9b2e6b06fa5a1b20dd59fcf85524abddebbc0c0f641170ac940e246e498b3</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:45:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T18:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deutsche-bank-under-fire-after-internal-documents-made-public/a-79974543--b2ac12e5d332.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deutsche-bank-under-fire-after-internal-documents-made-public/a-79974543?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A cache of internal records outlines the bank's dealings with Jeffrey Epstein, Donald Trump and Russian oligarchs. The German lender has sought to deflect criticism by claiming its bad behavior is a thing of the past.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Plans for Rwanda migrant hub come under fire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a83c314da5f3470adb35c61f927a1d56f1c81f102be8d415dd6f47c1a4c0d60c</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T10:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639--9c6685ac3d74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-plans-for-rwanda-migrant-hub-come-under-fire/live-79965639?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Human rights groups have slammed plans by Germany and four other EU states to send rejected asylum seekers to Rwanda. In other news, business start-ups in Germany are on track to reach the highest level since 2015.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany beat Netherlands 5-0 to win Nations League group</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9619b716270e63f9021ed6e98af5a474772ac1cb7ab0f84fa438f456b0f95b0</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T23:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-beat-netherlands-5-0-to-win-nations-league-group/a-79964394--6bc86424ecf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-beat-netherlands-5-0-to-win-nations-league-group/a-79964394?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Florian Wirtz scored twice as Germany cruised to a comfortable 5-0 win over the Netherlands to qualify for the Nations League quarter-finals on Monday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany joins 4 other EU states to set up Rwanda deportation hub</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16ec29d3a8e23099506bf5c8102c90299b0c5850ef6b2210c04642cf032ca082</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T12:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-joins-4-other-eu-states-to-set-up-rwanda-deportation-hub/a-79959158--227aa9c95b79.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-joins-4-other-eu-states-to-set-up-rwanda-deportation-hub/a-79959158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The move follows approval of EU regulations that ease deportations and allow hubs to be set up outside the bloc. A similar scheme by the UK government fell apart over legal issues though the US has one up and running.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz, Söder aim to revisit electricity tax cut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc939a7b4bad68cc83a1d6f37c0770b06c828948d987fe53a7d0fd9d292477c1</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-s_der-aim-to-revisit-electricity-tax-cut/live-79954869--6bc156ed2286.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-söder-aim-to-revisit-electricity-tax-cut/live-79954869?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Christian Democrats are in Munich, pushing to revive some tax relief that didn't make it into the budget after talks last week. And Manuela Schwesig faces a vote on a new term as regional leader. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tesla planning €3BN investment in German factory to produce Cybercabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd0f23821059ed0086dd03dfa6352701075b8b56e65b9a2b10be536fe46e7c89</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-_3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416--56a989627169.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tesla-planning-€3bn-investment-in-german-factory-to-produce-cybercabs/a-79961416?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Elon Musk-owned company is looking to further expand its only European production line. Brandenburg's state leader has welcomed the decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The AfD and neo-Nazi networks: How close are the connections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32d484b124507f057f26b2733e88aa17f1e96b26f74827cdefb90d1ba47e8853</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T16:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920--fb16f5d74381.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-afd-and-neo-nazi-networks-how-close-are-the-connections/a-79961920?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party (AfD) has become a focal point for the far right. Many of its members and staff have ties to ethnonationalist or neo-Nazi organizations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbb7c6c46a17bd745de97024d29acbb76b8c6752a403c112d0ae661cbe6cb874</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be802f4fbe22400806003fdff8c383adf8ff7b793e01664687487bfe0ae129a9</id><updated>2026-11-18T07:43:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
